    "result_text": "**Conclusion:** I reviewed the finding and respectfully declined it, leaving the code unchanged.\n\nThe finding recommends replacing the in-memory `isCustomerCodeInUse` scan with a repository-derived `existsByCustomerCode` query. While that's a valid Spring Data principle in general, it's the wrong call for this codebase:\n\n- **Local consistency wins:** all six sibling pre-save checks in `OwnerRestControllerV1` (including the near-identical `isIdentityKeyInUse`) scan `findAllOwners()` in memory; `ClinicService` exposes no `exists`/`count`/derived-query methods at all. My helper mirrors the established pattern exactly \u2014 the finding's approach would make it the odd one out.\n- **The efficiency rationale doesn't hold:** `addOwner` already calls `findAllOwners()` ~7 times per request, so one more scan is negligible, whereas a lone DB-side query would be threaded through the interface plus three profile-specific repository implementations for no consistency benefit.\n- The finding acknowledges this is structural/stylistic, not a correctness issue.\n\nAcceptance behaviour is untouched and the test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test passing).",
